# Everything here is excluded from the build context.
#
# This is not only about image size — the build context is uploaded to the
# daemon on every build, so a stray .venv (hundreds of MB) makes each build
# slower even when nothing is copied from it. It is also a security control:
# a .env in the context can be COPYed into a layer by accident, and layers are
# permanent even if a later step deletes the file.

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git/
.gitignore
.github/

*.md
!README.md

.DS_Store
